WEBVTT

00:03.134 --> 00:06.428
<i>That bore and I first met</i>

00:06.554 --> 00:09.014
<i>when I was in community college.</i>

00:09.682 --> 00:13.435
<i>He went to a fairly
prestigious college for our area.</i>

00:13.894 --> 00:18.148
<i>At the time, my friends
were infatuated with him.</i>

00:18.232 --> 00:20.317
<i>They called him broodingly sexy.</i>

00:20.651 --> 00:23.278
<i>Going out with him
made me feel superior.</i>

00:30.036 --> 00:31.704
<i>Then we had a child</i>

00:32.079 --> 00:35.916
Oh, so because it's three times
faster, the picture quality's…

00:37.793 --> 00:40.295
Hey, Hayato.
How about a "Hi, Mom"?

00:40.755 --> 00:41.881
Hi, Mom.

00:46.302 --> 00:49.138
<i>It's not that
my husband's a bad person.</i>

00:49.221 --> 00:51.556
<i>He's not even a heavy drinker.</i>

00:51.599 --> 00:54.310
<i>And while he doesn't bring home
a big paycheck,</i>

00:54.351 --> 00:55.602
<i>he's a hard worker.</i>

00:54.852 --> 00:58.647
KOSAKU KAWAJIRI
SHINOBU
HAYATO

00:55.895 --> 00:56.979
<i>But…</i>

00:57.063 --> 00:58.668
<i>I entered into marriage
with a complete stranger to love.</i>

01:01.984 --> 01:04.444
<i>Hmph. So he's finally home.</i>

01:04.612 --> 01:05.946
<i>All he ever says to me is,
"where's dinner,"</i>

01:05.988 --> 01:07.823
<i>"make me a bath,"
and "I'm going to bed."</i>

01:08.115 --> 01:10.575
<i>I'm married to a bore…</i>

01:20.211 --> 01:21.378
I'm home.

01:26.217 --> 01:27.676
Where's dinner?

01:28.260 --> 01:31.846
Oh, you're home?
I didn't even hear you come in.

01:31.889 --> 01:35.350
I was too busy to cook,
so that's all there is.

01:35.392 --> 01:37.268
But I got you your favorite.

01:38.854 --> 01:40.021
RAMEN
LAND

01:40.106 --> 01:41.690
<i>I wonder if he's pissed…</i>

01:41.774 --> 01:44.526
<i>If you've got the guts,
then show me what you got.</i>

01:44.610 --> 01:46.361
<i>Who am I kidding?</i>

01:46.403 --> 01:49.447
<i>You're gonna sit there stuffing your face
in silence like you always do.</i>

01:55.996 --> 01:59.666
<i>Good evening!
This is Morioh Radio.</i>

01:59.708 --> 02:02.460
<i>Kai Harada, here,
your neighborhood</i>

02:02.503 --> 02:03.879
<i>- purveyor of good vibes.</i>
- What are you doing?

02:03.921 --> 02:06.798
<i>And how is everyone
on this fine night?</i>

02:06.966 --> 02:09.885
<i>Allow me to ease you
into a mellow evening…</i>

02:10.928 --> 02:14.389
EPISODE 25
HEART FATHER

02:12.096 --> 02:14.411
<i>Fifteen minutes by car
from Morioh Station…</i>

02:15.224 --> 02:19.561
MORIOH STATION

02:15.391 --> 02:19.394
<i>in an area known for
its views and villas, is his house.</i>

02:16.183 --> 02:19.561
YOSHIKAGE KIRA'S HOUSE

02:20.104 --> 02:24.900
<i>Or I should say, it was his house,
when he was still Yoshikage Kira.</i>

02:23.566 --> 02:25.985
KIRA

02:26.318 --> 02:30.572
<i>He now has a new face,
a new family, a new job,</i>

02:30.656 --> 02:33.742
<i>a new place to call home.</i>

02:34.410 --> 02:36.745
<i>I'm sure he'll never
turn up here again.</i>

02:36.829 --> 02:38.831
- There's not a dead body
<i>- But we had no choice</i>

02:38.873 --> 02:40.332
- in the fridge, is there?
<i>- but to search the place.</i>

02:41.125 --> 02:45.003
<i>The only clues we're gonna
find to this new man's whereabouts,</i>

02:45.045 --> 02:48.465
<i>are gonna be right here
in this house.</i>

02:53.220 --> 02:54.930
Is that his album?

02:55.306 --> 02:57.432
Sure looks like him.

02:56.223 --> 02:59.100
THIRD GRADE
SUMMER CAMP
7-25-1974

02:57.516 --> 02:59.059
Yoshikage Kira…

02:59.101 --> 03:03.271
Born in Morioh, January 30th, 1966.

03:03.898 --> 03:06.942
He's 175 centimeters tall,
and weighs 65 kilograms.

03:07.026 --> 03:08.819
Blood type is A.

03:09.570 --> 03:12.114
He was born to older parents.

03:12.156 --> 03:15.826
He was 21 when his father,
Yoshihiro, fell ill and died.

03:16.285 --> 03:18.578
Seems his mother died
of old age soon after.

03:19.038 --> 03:22.875
In 1988, he graduated with
a degree in literature from D College.

03:23.334 --> 03:26.462
Same year, he became an employee of
Kameyu department store in S City.

03:26.629 --> 03:29.256
In 1993, he transferred to
the Morioh branch.

03:30.090 --> 03:34.135
He has no previous criminal record.
Never married. Has no close friends.

03:34.178 --> 03:36.889
Has no lover.
Never had any surgery.

03:36.931 --> 03:40.809
We have nothing to go by like fingerprints,
dental records, or surgical scars.

03:41.227 --> 03:43.812
Not a single lead anywhere.

03:44.146 --> 03:46.481
Look. These trophies and plaques…

03:46.523 --> 03:47.899
HIGH SCHOOL MUSIC RECITAL
VIOLIN
3RD PLACE
YOSHIKAGE KIRA

03:47.191 --> 03:48.734
They all say third place.

03:47.942 --> 03:49.610
MIDDLE SCHOOL TRACK
200 METER HURDLES
3RD PLACE
YOSHIKAGE KIRA

03:48.776 --> 03:51.153
He certainly wasn't
a star scholar-athlete.

03:49.652 --> 03:51.153
AWARD
GRADE SCHOOL
WRITING CONTEST
OVERALL 3RD PLACE

03:51.695 --> 03:54.239
Nothing speaks to his talents.

03:54.281 --> 03:56.658
Was it sports? Music? Writing?

03:57.284 --> 03:59.911
Even in this photo, he's doing
his best to not stand out.

03:59.995 --> 04:02.831
He's never been the object
of ridicule or envy…

04:02.957 --> 04:06.502
He reveals his strengths
and weaknesses to no one.

04:06.627 --> 04:07.711
Which means…

04:07.836 --> 04:09.212
It was clearly intentional.

04:09.296 --> 04:11.673
He was concealing his extraordinary
talent and intellect.

04:11.924 --> 04:15.010
He knew that was the best
way to stay out of trouble.

04:16.887 --> 04:18.346
My hope in coming here

04:18.430 --> 04:21.683
was to uncover his hobbies,
special interests, anything…

04:21.976 --> 04:24.353
Hobbies? Well I found…

04:24.561 --> 04:28.273
Seems he keeps a bunch
of jars in this drawer.

04:28.315 --> 04:29.232
See?

04:31.235 --> 04:34.613
Looks like a bunch
of bonito flakes.

04:34.780 --> 04:36.531
And what are these numbers?

04:36.824 --> 04:40.536
"1983" … Must be the year.

04:44.081 --> 04:46.875
They kinda stink.
What do you think they are?

04:46.917 --> 04:48.710
I think they're fingernail clippings.

04:48.961 --> 04:49.711
Huh?

04:52.715 --> 04:54.842
W-Whose nails
do you think they are?!

04:54.883 --> 04:56.384
Th-They couldn't be…

04:56.719 --> 05:00.639
No, they're his own.
They're not from his victims.

05:01.015 --> 05:03.726
He kept meticulous notes.

05:03.851 --> 05:06.436
Notes? You mean the numbers
on the jars?

05:06.603 --> 05:09.731
So he's been collecting
these things since 1983?

05:09.982 --> 05:11.817
For the past fifteen years?

05:11.734 --> 05:16.234
THUMB | INDEX FINGER |
MIDDLE FINGER | RING FINGER | PINKY
[NAIL GROWTH
GREATER THAN 30 cm, BY YEAR]
RIGHT HAND

05:12.109 --> 05:14.861
Gah! Every finger! The detail!

05:14.903 --> 05:17.655
So in 1983, his right thumb…

05:17.698 --> 05:20.617
grew a nail that was
31.5 centimeters long?

05:20.743 --> 05:25.243
1983 was the year
he murdered Reimi Sugimoto.

05:25.622 --> 05:27.749
The records begin
in that year.

05:28.000 --> 05:29.584
He reached an age

05:29.626 --> 05:32.503
where he could no longer
repress his murderous impulses.

05:33.047 --> 05:36.467
Whoa! The next page he's got
all the info on his toenails!

05:36.550 --> 05:37.968
Looks like
our unremarkable office worker

05:38.177 --> 05:40.387
has a rather remarkable hobby.

05:40.804 --> 05:44.140
NAIL GROWTH
GREATER THAN 30 cm, BY YEAR
KEEP UP THE GOOD WORK!!
NO ONE CAN STOP YOU.

05:44.641 --> 05:46.517
It's a form of divination.

05:46.560 --> 05:49.020
It's said Jewish merchants
observed sunspots

05:49.188 --> 05:51.857
to predict their economic prospects.

05:52.232 --> 05:54.609
Yoshikage Kira seems to
be tying his nail growth

05:54.735 --> 05:56.987
to his physical and
mental preparedness…

05:57.696 --> 06:00.156
His preparedness,
of course, to kill.

06:01.408 --> 06:03.118
1999!

06:03.202 --> 06:04.203
By June of this year,

06:04.244 --> 06:06.496
they'd already grown to
over 20 centimeters!

06:06.955 --> 06:09.415
He's crazy. He's sick!

06:09.583 --> 06:12.752
But this won't help us
track him down.

06:12.795 --> 06:14.338
There might be something else.

06:20.386 --> 06:24.886
Does this mean someone
else is in this house?

06:25.516 --> 06:28.143
Definitely seems that way.
Josuke, be prepared.

06:28.435 --> 06:30.728
Think he's got
a partner in crime?

06:30.896 --> 06:32.898
No… Not a chance.

06:32.940 --> 06:35.651
More people means more risk
for being caught.

06:35.734 --> 06:37.610
A partner could rat him out.

06:38.070 --> 06:40.280
There's nothing
he would mistrust more.

06:40.864 --> 06:42.115
This is…

06:42.449 --> 06:45.994
Mr. Jotaro, I'd like you
to take a look at that camera.

06:48.872 --> 06:51.833
I-It's his father… Kira's father!

06:51.917 --> 06:54.377
He's in the picture,
right behind us!

06:54.461 --> 06:55.462
But…

06:57.089 --> 07:01.009
Shit. We're in a shit load
of trouble.

07:01.218 --> 07:03.261
Does that mean he's a ghost?

07:03.303 --> 07:06.556
Yeah. Considering Reimi Sugimoto,

07:06.682 --> 07:09.476
it's possible his father is stuck
in a kind of spiritual limbo

07:09.518 --> 07:13.021
between the land of
the living and the dead.

07:13.939 --> 07:15.565
Look at his expression.

07:15.732 --> 07:18.609
Looks like he wants us
to make a quick exit.

07:18.777 --> 07:19.527
NUMBER WITHHELD
PUBLIC

07:24.491 --> 07:28.036
Are you trying to scare us
with your ghost energy?

07:28.162 --> 07:31.999
Something's starting to make it
really difficult for us to leave.

07:32.040 --> 07:34.375
<i>Get the lead out and
pick up the phone, slacker!</i>

07:34.460 --> 07:36.086
<i>I'm making it ring!</i>

07:42.342 --> 07:44.594
<i>You think that face
is telling you to leave?</i>

07:44.845 --> 07:46.429
<i>You're totally off, you moron!</i>

07:46.513 --> 07:51.013
<i>It's the face of a man who will
never let you leave this house!</i>

07:51.935 --> 07:54.228
<i>Go after my son,
and I'll make sure you die.</i>

07:54.354 --> 07:57.857
Dirty bastard! You know all about
the crimes your son has committed?

07:57.900 --> 08:01.320
Hey, something wrong?
What's with all the noise?

08:01.361 --> 08:02.695
Where are you?

08:02.738 --> 08:04.781
Show yourself,
you geriatric ghost!

08:05.699 --> 08:06.533
Ghost?!

08:09.536 --> 08:11.746
Josuke, he's not hiding.

08:11.914 --> 08:12.748
Huh?

08:12.831 --> 08:17.001
Looks like Kira's father
has been here with us all along.

08:17.044 --> 08:18.128
Look.

08:18.795 --> 08:19.587
BOOM

08:19.838 --> 08:21.798
Wha…? When did he…?

08:21.965 --> 08:24.258
He's moving around
in the picture.

08:24.343 --> 08:27.012
He called us from inside
the picture.

08:27.221 --> 08:30.015
He threw the phone at you
from this picture, too.

08:31.433 --> 08:33.977
<i>I'll kill you…</i>

08:34.811 --> 08:39.311
<i>Go after my dear son,
and I'll murder you!</i>

08:42.736 --> 08:43.778
Josuke!

08:44.446 --> 08:47.699
We can attack ghosts
with our Stands!

08:47.741 --> 08:52.120
Rohan-sensei used Heaven's Door
to read Reimi's memories!

08:52.204 --> 08:53.830
Bastard!

08:54.164 --> 08:55.498
Now what, creepy dick!

09:00.128 --> 09:01.671
What?!

09:05.676 --> 09:06.760
D-Damn!

09:06.802 --> 09:09.763
Damage inflicted on
the photograph backfires to us!

09:09.805 --> 09:11.097
Fix it now, Josuke!

09:11.139 --> 09:12.974
We'll be scattered to pieces!

09:18.730 --> 09:20.648
Josuke! Mr. Jotaro!

09:20.732 --> 09:23.526
<i>Those abilities…
Now I see!</i>

09:23.610 --> 09:24.402
<i>You two have</i>

09:24.444 --> 09:27.405
<i>special powers like my son!</i>

09:28.532 --> 09:30.825
Okuyasu, it's your turn now!

09:31.451 --> 09:35.496
Use The Hand to cut
that old man out of the picture!

09:36.707 --> 09:40.544
Gotcha! You put the job
in the right hands, Josuke!

09:41.920 --> 09:43.004
Huh?

09:45.340 --> 09:46.841
O-Okuyasu?

09:46.967 --> 09:48.969
W-What the—?!

09:49.011 --> 09:52.014
How did I run straight
into the window?

09:55.392 --> 09:59.104
M-My hands are coming out
all the way over there!

09:59.146 --> 10:02.065
Something's keeping me
from entering the room!

10:05.110 --> 10:06.361
That's…

10:07.988 --> 10:09.364
A-A wall!

10:09.406 --> 10:12.242
There's some kind of
invisible wall right here!

10:12.409 --> 10:14.911
I can't break it! No!

10:15.120 --> 10:17.372
Finally figured it out, eh?

10:18.165 --> 10:20.041
That's the edge of the photo!

10:20.125 --> 10:24.625
You may think you're in the room,
but you're not.

10:25.964 --> 10:29.550
I'm a ghost living in a photograph…

10:29.593 --> 10:33.179
I can control the space of
any photograph in which I appear.

10:33.472 --> 10:35.056
With that camera,

10:35.140 --> 10:38.560
I can confine a person's spiritual
energy within a photograph!

10:38.852 --> 10:40.979
That's my special little trick!

10:41.021 --> 10:42.897
That room is inside the picture!

10:42.981 --> 10:45.733
If you damage the photo,
you damage the spiritual energy too,

10:45.817 --> 10:49.237
effectively causing
grave harm to yourselves!

10:49.488 --> 10:53.867
We're inside the picture?
I'm looking right at it!

10:53.950 --> 10:56.077
<i>You're clearly a bit on
the dim side,</i>

10:56.119 --> 10:57.620
<i>so let me spell it out for you.</i>

10:57.704 --> 10:59.539
After I kill those two,

10:59.581 --> 11:03.251
I'll ensnare the both of you
and shred you to pieces!

11:04.711 --> 11:07.630
J-Josuke! Jotaro!

11:10.217 --> 11:12.886
I'll kill you…

11:12.928 --> 11:15.639
You bastard! Stop, damn it!

11:16.223 --> 11:18.433
Jotaro, what are you doing?

11:18.475 --> 11:22.312
Do something with your super
strong Star Platinum!

11:23.021 --> 11:25.523
Josuke… I've thrown in the towel.

11:25.691 --> 11:26.441
Huh?

11:26.566 --> 11:29.777
Stopping that old-timer's attacks
is downright impossible.

11:29.861 --> 11:33.364
If every bit of damage we deal him
comes right back to us,

11:33.407 --> 11:36.535
then stopping time with
Star Platinum is useless.

11:37.744 --> 11:39.746
If it's pointless, I don't bother.

11:39.996 --> 11:42.873
I can't believe what
I'm hearing, Mr. Jotaro.

11:43.500 --> 11:45.543
What the fudge are you saying?!

11:45.919 --> 11:50.419
I'll kill you!

11:57.764 --> 12:00.433
Your heads got some good spin!

12:01.476 --> 12:02.768
H-He's got a knife…

12:08.066 --> 12:08.816
What?!

12:09.651 --> 12:12.278
I can't touch it! Mr. Jotaro!

12:12.696 --> 12:14.781
I've given up on
stopping the geezer.

12:15.323 --> 12:16.407
But…

12:17.701 --> 12:18.618
Wha—?

12:21.329 --> 12:25.041
If he really controls
any photograph he's in…

12:26.960 --> 12:30.213
then maybe all we have to do
is take a picture of him by himself,

12:30.297 --> 12:31.881
so he's alone.

12:33.133 --> 12:34.676
What?!

12:39.097 --> 12:43.434
You managed to sidestep
my attack… Blast it!

12:43.477 --> 12:45.729
Josuke, leave 'em with
some words of wisdom.

12:45.854 --> 12:47.856
Stick 'em with
a little style!

12:49.608 --> 12:52.986
Y-You weren't so scary after all,
you big dumb idiot!

12:57.324 --> 13:00.035
THE HAND

13:00.327 --> 13:01.536
Damn you!

13:01.620 --> 13:04.122
So you're seasoned fighters
I see.

13:04.164 --> 13:06.958
You have battled foes
like my son

13:07.000 --> 13:09.293
over and over again,
haven't you!

13:09.586 --> 13:13.047
The dick can get out,
cause he's a ghost, remember…

13:21.681 --> 13:24.433
We need to make sure you
stay put and behave yourself.

13:24.893 --> 13:29.230
There's something in this house
you really don't want us to find.

13:29.523 --> 13:31.691
That's why you attacked us.

13:41.827 --> 13:43.286
I get it.

13:43.370 --> 13:46.623
So if you fold him in half,
there's no way he can get out.

13:46.706 --> 13:48.624
He can't run away.

13:48.917 --> 13:50.835
Okuyasu and Koichi,
you've got this room.

13:50.877 --> 13:52.545
We'll search the right side.

13:55.215 --> 13:58.801
I can't protect
my son like this! Damn it!

13:58.885 --> 14:01.095
If it falls into their hands…

14:09.896 --> 14:12.189
But what in the world is it
do you think

14:12.232 --> 14:13.942
that he doesn't want us to find?

14:13.984 --> 14:16.945
I'm not sweating it.

14:17.028 --> 14:20.406
If Kira's old man there turns white
as a ghost, then we should be good.

14:20.615 --> 14:23.075
I-I can't breathe…

14:23.493 --> 14:27.413
I-It's torture…
Please, just a little.

14:27.581 --> 14:31.209
Just poke some holes
in the tape and let me breathe…

14:31.293 --> 14:33.962
Y-You really can't breathe?

14:34.004 --> 14:36.965
Hey, Koichi,
he's pulling your leg.

14:37.048 --> 14:39.300
He wants you to make
an opening so he can escape.

14:39.384 --> 14:43.596
I know you don't believe me,
b-but I'm really dying in here!

14:43.638 --> 14:45.765
Well, I am claustrophobic,

14:45.807 --> 14:48.810
so I guess I do sorta
get how he feels…

14:48.894 --> 14:52.814
Oh, quit bitching. So you really
want a breathing hole, eh?

14:52.856 --> 14:56.359
Fine. I'll give you
some breathing holes…

14:56.902 --> 14:58.862
With a bunch of tacks.

14:58.945 --> 15:00.655
W-What are you doing?!

15:01.907 --> 15:05.660
Damn it! Get me out of here,
you wretched little punk!

15:05.702 --> 15:07.370
There he is.

15:08.580 --> 15:10.915
Those tacks aren't
going anywhere.

15:10.999 --> 15:13.084
Tacks? I'm blind as a bat,

15:13.126 --> 15:14.877
but if my guess is right,
they stuck me to the post.

15:16.796 --> 15:18.839
Which gives me a great idea!

15:18.882 --> 15:23.303
You don't realize it, but those tacks
are my ticket out of here!

15:24.596 --> 15:27.348
And it couldn't be simpler!
Much obliged!

15:27.432 --> 15:29.976
So long, suckers!

15:30.435 --> 15:32.061
Wha…?!

15:35.523 --> 15:37.358
Hey, you bastard…

15:37.400 --> 15:40.778
What was that sound?
What did you do?

15:42.155 --> 15:44.490
Say something, damn it!

15:44.532 --> 15:48.285
O-Okuyasu, now we're really in a mess!
I think he just ran away!

15:49.537 --> 15:52.248
Jotaro! H-He broke loose!

15:52.791 --> 15:57.291
I-It's my fault. I stuck some
tacks in it, and then he did something!

16:02.509 --> 16:04.719
You've been duped, dummy!

16:04.844 --> 16:08.013
I just psyched you out and won.

16:08.848 --> 16:10.558
What?!

16:14.854 --> 16:16.480
Th-This is…

16:16.523 --> 16:18.483
What's this doing here?

16:18.525 --> 16:19.526
It can't be!

16:19.567 --> 16:23.153
It's the bow and arrow…
But we already got them…

16:24.322 --> 16:28.367
I thought the Speedwagon Foundation
was keeping them safe and sound…

16:28.410 --> 16:29.828
There's another set?

16:29.869 --> 16:33.080
Josuke, watch out!
Kira's father escaped!

16:35.834 --> 16:36.584
What?!

16:36.668 --> 16:39.587
With this very arrow,
Yoshikage's Deadly Queen was born!

16:39.671 --> 16:41.756
The real game-changer
is the arrow!

16:41.798 --> 16:44.133
I'll never surrender the arrow!

16:57.063 --> 17:00.107
R-Reverb, Koichi!
Sick Act 1 on him!

17:00.525 --> 17:02.652
I can't, he's too far away!

17:02.736 --> 17:04.154
I can't believe this…

17:04.237 --> 17:08.737
So what Kira's father didn't want us
to find was the bow and arrow!

17:11.286 --> 17:13.788
D-Damn it!
It's all my fault!

17:13.872 --> 17:17.125
No, Okuyasu.
He was the superior opponent.

17:17.292 --> 17:20.878
There's no mistaking Kira is his son.

17:21.212 --> 17:23.464
It's their unrelenting tenacity

17:23.548 --> 17:26.467
to survive at all costs that
got the best of us.

17:29.554 --> 17:32.473
As long as they don't get
this arrow, we'll be fine.

17:32.515 --> 17:36.060
This little beauty will
make even more enemies for them!

17:36.394 --> 17:39.188
The bow and arrow, huh…
I see.

17:39.481 --> 17:42.108
I thought there might
be more than one set.

17:42.650 --> 17:44.568
That explains how
DIO and his henchmen

17:44.611 --> 17:48.656
were able to pull together such
a large group of Stand users so quickly.

17:49.282 --> 17:51.492
With multiple sets of
bows and arrows,

17:51.534 --> 17:53.869
they built an army of minions
across the globe.

17:55.872 --> 18:00.251
Kira's father probably
obtained this set from Enyaba the witch,

18:00.293 --> 18:03.504
and eventually,
Okuyasu's brother, Keicho,

18:03.588 --> 18:07.383
got a hold of one, too,
before arriving in this town.

18:08.301 --> 18:12.013
Stand users really do seem
to be drawn to each other.

18:13.098 --> 18:16.684
Yoshikage, where are you?

18:16.810 --> 18:18.269
Even as a little boy,

18:18.311 --> 18:20.855
you couldn't repress
your urges to kill women.

18:21.231 --> 18:25.731
But if that's what makes you happy,
I'll support and protect you.

18:26.653 --> 18:27.445
You are…

18:30.240 --> 18:34.619
my one and only son.

18:34.911 --> 18:37.121
KOSAKU KAWAJIRI
SHINOBU
HAYATO

18:39.249 --> 18:43.628
What's with the change of heart?
You're actually cooking?

18:43.670 --> 18:45.630
How is that even possible…

18:46.506 --> 18:48.925
Two plates? This one's for me?

18:49.008 --> 18:52.261
You want me to eat
something you cooked?

18:52.428 --> 18:53.887
Are you insane?

18:56.850 --> 19:00.645
Hey! Cut your nails later!

19:00.937 --> 19:03.773
Didn't you just cut them
last night?

19:03.857 --> 19:05.608
They sure grow fast…

19:12.991 --> 19:16.452
<i>Oh… It actually tastes amazing…</i>

19:25.795 --> 19:28.589
HEART FATHER

19:33.386 --> 19:34.887
A little kitty cat!

19:35.805 --> 19:37.264
What's wrong?

19:37.891 --> 19:40.351
Were you crying all night
at the top of that tree

19:40.393 --> 19:41.936
because you couldn't get in?

19:42.562 --> 19:45.731
Hey! You closed that damn
window near the tree, didn't you?!

19:47.901 --> 19:51.154
I've told you over and over
not to shut it!

19:54.115 --> 19:57.076
What's wrong, kitty?
Why are you so worked up?

20:06.085 --> 20:08.629
Cats hate water.

20:08.755 --> 20:12.258
My apologies. I wasn't thinking.

20:12.759 --> 20:14.218
I won't do it again.

20:17.430 --> 20:20.975
<i>Something's strange.
Something strange is going on with him.</i>

20:21.100 --> 20:23.644
<i>He suddenly starts cooking
for me,</i>

20:23.686 --> 20:27.690
<i>and now, he's using an actual blade
instead of his electric razor.</i>

20:27.857 --> 20:29.859
<i>Blades always give him razor burn…</i>

20:31.444 --> 20:35.489
Hey, you still haven't paid
last month's rent.

20:35.531 --> 20:37.908
Including this month,
you now owe me 260,000 yen.

20:37.951 --> 20:39.369
Pay up right now!

20:41.537 --> 20:42.621
Rent?

20:43.748 --> 20:47.501
You heard him.
Go get the money from the safe.

20:48.378 --> 20:49.462
The safe?

20:50.046 --> 20:53.841
Hurry! You're the only one who
knows the combination to the safe!

20:58.805 --> 21:01.098
Hey, what are you…

21:02.433 --> 21:04.935
Thank you for coming
so early in the morning, sir.

21:05.061 --> 21:09.023
But I seem to be a bit
short on cash right now.

21:09.691 --> 21:10.566
Huh?

21:10.650 --> 21:12.360
I'm not playing around!

21:12.402 --> 21:14.028
I should've known
you wouldn't be able to afford

21:14.070 --> 21:18.570
my gorgeous home with
that pathetic salary, you schmuck!

21:19.575 --> 21:22.035
Learn to live within your means!

21:23.329 --> 21:26.707
- Right away—
- No, I think you misunderstood.

21:26.833 --> 21:29.377
When I said
I was a bit short, look.

21:29.460 --> 21:32.963
I meant that I had only
a little over 500,000 yen.

21:34.257 --> 21:35.967
I'll only be able to pay
for this month,

21:36.009 --> 21:39.053
last month, and the next
two months in advance.

21:39.512 --> 21:40.846
Will that suffice?

21:41.139 --> 21:43.224
Well, yes I…

21:43.433 --> 21:45.560
Thank you very much.

21:46.602 --> 21:48.312
Until next time!

21:49.731 --> 21:51.274
Y-You…

21:53.026 --> 21:56.029
You must have stolen that
money from the landlord.

21:56.154 --> 21:58.406
I don't know how you did it,

21:58.531 --> 22:01.075
but you stole it from his bag,
didn't you?

22:02.702 --> 22:04.912
<i>Most people in this situation…</i>

22:04.954 --> 22:08.123
<i>would be filled with
fear and disgust…</i>

22:08.666 --> 22:13.166
<i>But his gusto…
The way he stole the money…</i>

22:13.338 --> 22:17.050
<i>This person,
after so many years together,</i>

22:17.091 --> 22:19.635
<i>for the first time, he makes me…</i>

22:21.554 --> 22:25.182
<i>He's awakened in me
pangs of romantic passion…</i>

23:38.214 --> 23:41.425
EPISODE 26
ROSHAM BOY IS HERE!
